        {
          "page": "2",
          "section": "2. Experimental procedures",
          "quote": "The initial HEA powders were synthesized by MA between elemental powders (purity > 99.9%, particle size < 45 µm), and the entire process was operated utilizing a high-energy ball-milling apparatus protected by argon at 250 r/min. Thirty-hour dry milling was used to achieve a pre-solid solution between the elements, while six-hour wet milling with the control agent (ethanol) acted as the grain-refining process.",
          "table": null,
          "figure": null,
          "chunk_id": "28554f6f4e95160d:part:001"
